  R1.stopper.look_ring narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    An empty rope clamp. The rope is fastened to the plate's ring at the bend now. There it runs above the water to the far bank. They're holding it there.
  agata:H2d.nina_mirror.clamp_early agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The sluice first — Pavel's waiting by the winch. Once we've drained the water, I'll see to the mirror.
  agata:H1.after_mirror.agata agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    [surprised] I did, Tikhon. While I sleep one night, Mama will live a whole week… How can I sleep now?
  agata:O4.nina_house.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Mama's house. The same porch — only the step has been replaced.
  agata:O4.ilya_house.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Ilya's house, at the edge. Mitya knocked on that shutter.
  agata:O4.river.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The river below, and the far pier. I followed Mitya's lantern up from there.
  agata:O3.bed.early_d2 agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    My bed — Mama never put it away. But it's too early to lie down.
  agata:O3.bed.late_d2 agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    It's late. Ulya and I will share — we'll make room.
  agata:O3.clock.look_common agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Keeping time with my watch — minute for minute.
  agata:O3.clock.watch agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    I compare them: my second hand and the pendulum move in step. Minute for minute.
  agata:O3.notebooks.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    A stack of notebooks, filled in Dunya's hand. How much she wrote…
  agata:O3.notebooks.use agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Eighteen years trying to restore the road. So many notebooks… Every one filled in her own hand.
  agata:O3.notebooks.again agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Dunya's notebooks. I'll read them again.
  agata:O3.village_list.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The names of the whole village, on one sheet. Mama wrote them down.
  agata:O3.village_list.use agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Twenty-two alive. Fifteen of the original eighteen remain; seven were born here. Three died. Dunya among them.
  agata:O3.village_list.again agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The residents' list. Twenty-two people alive.
  agata:O3.notches.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Yearly notches — someone else's height. Ulyana was measured every year. Mine were here too, lower down.
  agata:E5.windlass.voice_call_lower agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Go!
  agata:E5.windlass.voice_call_stop agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Stop!
  agata:E5.windlass.voice_call_raise agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Raise!
  agata:O1d.ulyana.hat_a agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    I did. I was eight, just like you. Mama saw it, but didn't rub it off. Let the bird be warm, she said.
  agata:O1d.ulyana.lights_a agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    He was waiting for a light from our bank. All twenty of your years.
  agata:O1d.ulyana.lights_c agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Not again, Ulya. I promise.
  agata:O4.mitya.fish_q agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Mitya, do you fish?
  agata:O1d.ulyana.ttt_q agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Ulya, shall we play noughts and crosses? In chalk, right on the board.
  agata:O4.mitya_board.use agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Twenty notches — one for every winter Mitya stood by the lantern. I should give it to him.
  agata:O3.nina.ribbon_again agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The ribbon in my braid. Just as before.
  agata:O3.nina_letters.look agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    A bundle of letters tied with string on the chest of drawers. My name on every one.
  agata:O3.nina_letters.use agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Mama wrote to me every winter. Twenty letters, with nowhere to send them.
  agata:O3.nina_letters.again agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Mama's letters from twenty winters.
  agata:H1d.nina_coat.use agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The sleeve seam's split. I'll mend it — it should hang here at home, in one piece.
  agata:O1q.village_map.use agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    We drew this map as a class. There's the house at the edge — Ilya's now. Beside it, just a fence and empty space.
  agata:O1q.village_map.agata_help agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Help me find it, then. How do I get to your house?
  agata:O1q.village_map.agata_mark agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    I'll mark the tracing paper: school, your house, then the garden.
  agata:O1q.village_map.traced agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Currants grow there now.
  O4q.workshop.prompt narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Where shall the second bench go?
  agata:examine.brace_plate agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    Heavy, forged iron. Dunya bent it to follow the crack in the plate exactly.
  agata:examine.bell_clapper agata     ru           Agata      eleven_v4    The mill bell's clapper. Without it, the bell is mute.
